<h2>Indian garlic for export</h2>
<p>We can supply fresh Indian garlic, sourced primarily from Madhya Pradesh — India's largest garlic-producing state, centred on the Neemuch–Mandsaur–Ratlam belt — with additional volume from Gujarat and Rajasthan.</p>

<h2>An honest note on scale</h2>
<p>Fresh garlic is a genuinely small part of India's export trade — the country's total fresh garlic exports run in the single-digit millions of US dollars a year, dwarfed by China's dominant position in world garlic trade. We say this upfront rather than overselling volume or availability: garlic is available from us, priced and supplied against your order, but it isn't a flagship high-volume line the way onion or our dehydrated onion/garlic powder are. If your requirement is for larger, more price-competitive volumes, <a href="/products/fresh-vegetables/red-onion/">red onion</a> or a dehydrated garlic powder specification may suit better — ask us to quote both.</p>

<h2>How should I specify garlic?</h2>
<ul>
  <li><strong>Size grade.</strong> 35–45mm, 45–55mm or 55mm+ bulb diameter are the common export bands.</li>
  <li><strong>Curing.</strong> Properly cured garlic with dry outer skin is essential for transit survival, the same principle that applies to onion.</li>
</ul>

<h2>Pricing</h2>
<p>Send your grade, quantity and destination port and we'll confirm current availability and quote FOB/CIF terms.</p>

